# Cursor Rules for God-Tier macOS Development Environment

## Entry Points
- AGENTS.md - AI instructions (start here)
- llms.txt - Documentation index
- CLAUDE.md - AI assistant context
- docs/WORKFLOWS.md - Task execution steps

## Project Type
macOS Development Environment. Mise-first orchestration.

## Tool Hierarchy
Mise > Bun > Pixi > Uv

## Critical Rules
- NEVER use sudo - Everything is user-space
- NEVER install globally with npm/pip - Use mise (`mise use -g`)
- NEVER modify system Python/Node - Mise manages versions
- NEVER commit secrets - Use op://, infisical, or mise secrets
- ALWAYS use mise tasks - Not raw commands (`mise run validate`)
- ALWAYS run tests before committing - `bats tests/`

## Common Commands
- mise run validate - Check environment health
- mise run tools:status - Show all tools and settings
- mise doctor - Diagnose issues
- bats tests/ - Run all tests

## Do Not
- Use sudo for any installation
- Install packages globally (npm -g, pip install)
- Modify files outside project directory
- Commit .env files or API keys
- Suppress TypeScript errors with `as any` or `@ts-ignore`

## Key Files
- config/mise.toml - Tool versions, tasks, settings (SOURCE OF TRUTH)
- tests/*.bats - 254 BATS tests
- setup.sh - Bootstrap script
